{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch79SQ536vx88B8tAXmgf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I left out the line that every other publisher pays at least $12,000, because your own facts don't back it up. You have one $12,500 fee, and your agent's range starts at $11,000. If the publisher knows the market or asks for examples, that claim could hurt your credibility. The true numbers are strong enough without it, and they make $11,500 look like a reasonable ask.\n\nFill in the bracketed parts before sending.\n\n<final_document>\nSubject: Fee for [Book Title]\n\nHi [Editor's name],\n\nThank you for offering me [Book Title]. I'd love to illustrate it, and I've really valued working with you and the team over the past four years.\n\nBefore I confirm, I'd like to talk about the fee. I've been paid $9,000 per book since our first project together, and a lot has changed since then. Of the six books we've made, two have each sold more than 20,000 copies, and [Title] was chosen for the [State] reading list. Each book also takes me about four months of full-time work.\n\nMy fees elsewhere have gone up as well. Last year another publisher paid me $12,500 for a 32-page book of the same scope. My agent tells me that $11,000 to $13,000 is the usual range for an illustrator with my track record.\n\nFor this book, I'm asking for $11,500. That's toward the lower end of that range, because I value working with you and want to keep making books together.\n\nI'm happy to talk it over on a call if that's easier. I'm looking forward to getting started.\n\nBest,\n[Your name]\n</final_document>"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5373,"cache_read_input_tokens":3853,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5373},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"s